# Editor and OS noise
*.bak
*.bak-*
.DS_Store

# Sandbox bookkeeping the Claude Code sandbox writes into the repo root. Not
# part of the package — but .claude/skills/ holds real project skills (the
# release process), so that one is tracked deliberately.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.mcp.json

# Compiled Python. Running the skill writes these into whatever directory it
# loaded from, including a --link install, where that directory is this repo.
# manifest.sh ignores them when it checks the live tree for the same reason.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Where bin/notes.sh promote parks a project's tooling findings until someone
# folds them into reference/. Work in progress, not payload.
skill/reference/staging/

# This repo drives an app too, so it has a conf of its own — and the conf is the
# one file the package tells every project to keep out of version control,
# because it is where a credential goes (bin/config.sh, "project values"). It
# holds none today, which is exactly why this belongs here now: bin/secrets.sh
# only checks the file is gitignored once a project value exists, so the first
# APP_PIN written into it would arrive in an untracked, unignored file that a
# `git add -A` sweeps straight in.
#
# The second line is the PROFILE layering: PROFILE=uat reads
# .maestro-mac.conf.uat, and per-environment confs are where APP_PIN, APP_STORE
# and APP_USER actually live.
.maestro-mac.conf
.maestro-mac.conf.*
